<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        Inspections, BIM and Work Progress (which carries RA and milestone billing) are premium
        modules: the Free plan keeps Toolbox Talks only, and STARTER, PRO and ENTERPRISE keep all four.

        The earlier seeds granted these three on every plan, including FREE, so this removes just those
        three FREE grants. It is a new changeSet rather than an edit to the applied ones: their
        DATABASECHANGELOG keys and checksums stay as they are, and a fresh database still runs them in
        order and then this one. The file sits in this directory because includeAll runs modules/ in path
        order, and bim/002 and work-progress/002 must already have granted FREE before this takes it away.
        (inspections is seeded earlier, in v4.0/096.)

        Nothing is deleted besides the plan_feature rows: an organization's inspections, models and
        schedule stay in place, and are refused by the entitlement gate while it is on a plan without the
        module. The delete matches by plan and feature code through sub-selects, so it needs no vendor
        syntax, does nothing on a database that has no FREE plan or no such grants, and gives the same
        result when run twice. A plan or feature code that does not exist matches no row, so it cannot
        stop boot.
    -->

    <changeSet id="work-progress-003-revoke-premium-modules-from-free" author="echno">
        <sql>
            DELETE FROM plan_feature
            WHERE plan_id IN (SELECT id FROM plan WHERE code = 'FREE')
              AND feature_id IN (SELECT id FROM feature
                                 WHERE code IN ('MODULE_INSPECTIONS', 'MODULE_BIM', 'MODULE_WORK_PROGRESS'))
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql>
                INSERT INTO plan_feature (plan_id, feature_id, enabled)
                SELECT p.id, f.id, true
                FROM plan p, feature f
                WHERE p.code = 'FREE'
                  AND f.code IN ('MODULE_INSPECTIONS', 'MODULE_BIM', 'MODULE_WORK_PROGRESS')
                  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM plan_feature x WHERE x.plan_id = p.id AND x.feature_id = f.id)
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
